Package: OpenPVA
Title: Composable Individual-Based Population Viability Analysis
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Barry W.", "Brook", email = "bwbrook@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: An execution engine for individual-based population viability
    analysis in which a life cycle is a direct ordered list of ordinary R
    process objects. Each process declares the state fields it requires,
    writes and creates. The engine owns time, identifiers, replicate
    random-number streams, cohort-level accounting, exact pedigree
    inbreeding coefficients and provenance. Reusable processes cover
    survival, reproduction with several litter-size distributions, pairing
    and territory limits, removals, introductions, environmental variation,
    catastrophes, density feedback and inbreeding depression. Ensemble
    helpers separate structural and parametric designs from Monte Carlo
    replicates and report viability summaries with Monte Carlo standard
    errors.
